cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GESTURE-FX: Gesture-Triggered Camera Effects in the Browser
message: >-
  If you use this software or the gesture detection method it introduces, please
  cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Amey
    family-names: Thakur
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5644-1575'

repository-code: 'https://github.com/Amey-Thakur/GESTURE-FX'
url: 'https://amey-thakur.github.io/GESTURE-FX/'

abstract: >-
  GESTURE-FX is a browser application that recognises hand gestures in a live
  camera feed and composites a visual effect onto the video at the instant the
  gesture occurs, producing a finished recording that requires no editing.

  It introduces a geometric method for detecting a palm flip that requires no
  trained classifier. The two dimensional cross product of the two palm edges,
  taken at the wrist and normalised by their lengths, is the sine of the angle
  between those edges as projected onto the image, signed by the winding order of
  the triangle they span. Rotating a hand past edge-on reverses that winding and
  drives the magnitude to zero, so a flip is a zero crossing of a single scalar
  and the crossing identifies the exact frame of the gesture. The method is
  provably invariant to image mirroring, to hand scale and to handedness, and
  requires no calibration or training data.

  Detection, stylisation and recording run entirely on the client. Landmark
  inference is decoupled from rendering, so effect playback is independent of
  tracking throughput, and the recorder captures the composited canvas so the
  effect is present in the exported file as pixels. Two auxiliary features are
  exceptions and are disabled by default: spoken command recognition, which uses
  the browser's own speech interface, and an optional delegated restyle, which
  sends one recording to a hosted model against a key the user supplies.

